13	// Message ids are arbitrary byte strings: the Go submit interface accepts any
14	// non-empty id without requiring valid UTF-8 — Chinese text, whitespace,
15	// colons, NUL bytes, stray 0xFF/0xFE bytes, or text mixed with them. Identity
16	// is judged by the exact bytes: the single bytes 0xFF and 0xFE and the legal
17	// character U+FFFD are three different ids. JSON string encoding silently
18	// rewrites invalid UTF-8 to U+FFFD, so without byte-exact persistence the
19	// original id would lose its message after a reopen and two distinct ids
20	// could replay as duplicate submits, making the directory unopenable.
